{
  "requirement": "The `Tsx` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct Tsx;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Tsx;\nimpl Debug for Tsx;\nimpl Default for Tsx;\nimpl OutlineLang for Tsx;\nimpl Copy for Tsx;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.typescript.Tsx`.\n\n**Obligations.** The requirement says `Tsx` is a public struct. It lists `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang` and `Copy`. The `OutlineLang` impl supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules.\n\n**Implementation shape.** `Tsx` is generated by the `language!` macro in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs`, invoked as `language!(Tsx, typescript::TSX_PROFILE, \"tsx-structural-v1\")`. The macro applies `#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]` to a unit struct.\n\n**Coverage.**\n- **Extensions and scheme:** `bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline` calls `check(languages::Tsx, \"a.TSX\", \"function check() { return <div />; }\", \"function[check]\", &[\"tsx\"], \"tsx-structural-v1\")`.\n  - It asserts `extensions()` equals `[\"tsx\"]`, `fingerprint_scheme()` equals `\"tsx-structural-v1\"`, and `name()` is non-empty.\n  - Extension claiming is checked through `from_source` with the upper-cased extension `.TSX`.\n- **Selection:** the same test asserts that `select(\"function[check]\")` succeeds. It also checks that the inferred and explicit outlines have the same selectors, diagnostic and fingerprint, and that the root item has selector `\"\"` and spans the whole source.\n- **Fingerprint:** it compares the inferred and explicit fingerprints and the scheme. The detailed fingerprint rules belong to `requirements.sdk.sources.typescript.fingerprints`, which has its own tests.\n- **Trait set:**\n  - `check` is bounded by `L: OutlineLang + Default + Copy`, so `Tsx` must implement `Default`, `Copy` and `OutlineLang`.\n  - It calls `Clone::clone`, asserts that the clone's extensions match the original, and calls `L::default().fingerprint_scheme()`.\n  - It asserts the type has zero size.\n  - It also exercises `search_structure` on the Tsx source.\n- **TSX-specific outlines:** `typescript_and_tsx_share_signatures_abstract_classes_and_module_kinds` checks `api.tsx` against the exact selector list and shows the TSX items match the `.ts` items. This covers outline selection for TSX files.\n- **Public export:** `public_exports_match_the_appendix` checks that the public export inventory matches rustdoc. That covers `Tsx` being a public struct.\n\n**Debug.** No test formats `Debug` output. The impl is a pure `derive` with no conditional and no custom transformation, and the requirement states no particular output. It needs no test of its own, so this is not a gap.\n\n**Marking.** The tests carry `{test}` references to the subject, so there is no marking gap.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
